# Intentionally no rules.
#
# This used to hold the SPA catch-all `/*  /index.html  200`. It is gone
# because the build now writes a real HTML file per route (about.html,
# services/b2b/email-marketing.html, ...) carrying that page's title,
# description and link-preview tags, and a catch-all would serve every
# visitor the homepage's file instead.
#
# The SPA fallback for anything else is still in place natively:
#   - Workers (current host): `not_found_handling: single-page-application`
#     in wrangler.jsonc.
#   - Pages: with no top-level 404.html, Pages treats the project as an
#     SPA and serves index.html for unmatched paths.
